    <string name="onboarding_welcome_title">Every other weather app is **polite** about it</string>
    <string name="onboarding_welcome_body">This one tells you the forecast and then says what it really thinks. Nobody asked for the opinion. You are getting it anyway.</string>

    <string name="onboarding_quips_title">The forecast comes with **commentary**</string>
    <string name="onboarding_quips_body">Rain means the sky is having a meltdown. A heatwave means the pavement is melting under your feet. Drag the screen up when you want the boring numbers instead.</string>

    <string name="onboarding_location_title">We need to know **where** you are suffering</string>
    <string name="onboarding_location_body">Location access is how the app knows which sky to insult. Precise pins your neighbourhood, approximate settles for your region — honestly, both are fine for weather. Your coordinates only go to the services that fetch your weather and your town\'s name. Nowhere else.</string>
